# Copy this file to .env.local (which stays gitignored) and fill in values.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keystatic GitHub mode (optional)
#
# Without these, the /keystatic editor runs in `local` storage mode: no login,
# saves write straight into the working tree of the machine running `next dev`.
#
# With them set, the editor runs `github` mode: OAuth login, editors need repo
# write access, and saves are committed to keystatic/* branches. The
# docs-editor-pr workflow then opens a PR so editor changes get the same
# review + drift-check gates as a human PR.
#
# Easiest way to generate all four: run `npm run dev`, visit
# http://localhost:3000/keystatic/setup, and it writes them into .env.local
# for you. Only the repo owner needs to do this once; editors just log in.
# See /docs/contributing for the full description of the two modes.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Slug of the GitHub App created by /keystatic/setup (also read client-side,
# hence NEXT_PUBLIC_)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=

# OAuth client credentials from that GitHub App
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Secret used to sign the editor's OAuth session cookie (any random string)
# KEYSTATIC_SECRET=
